      "decision": "reject",
      "reason": "The symptoms presented, such as progressive abdominal pain, constipation, vomiting, and upper abdominal distention with tympany, do not strictly align with the typical presentation of Superior Mesenteric Artery Syndrome, which usually involves compression of the duodenum leading to symptoms like postprandial abdominal pain and vomiting. The evidence provided does not strongly support Superior Mesenteric Artery Syndrome as a Gastrointestinal Motility Disorder in this context."
    },
